            <ArticleTitle>Cauda equina syndrome following traction for acute sciatica.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>370-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case report of a patient who developed cauda equina syndrome following pelvic traction for acute sciatica is presented. A good outcome was obtained with prompt surgical decompression. This case illustrates the potential dangers of traction, which is frequently employed in the management of acute back pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
